lisa-design:
SeedPath continuity ids are the LITERAL plugin-path + "/" + file (not path.Join) — design §13.4 R77 correction (round-3 agent review). Non-identity ids: seedFile = path.Clean(id) (matches OPA's cleaned policy_file); seedPolicyPath = strings.TrimSuffix(rawID, "/"+rel) when the raw id ends in "/"+rel (rel = policyFile relative to path.Clean(policyPath)), else rawID. This reproduces legacy seeds for local sources with non-clean paths (./policies, x/, /abs/p/). Identity ids (id == file or Clean(id) == file) still return the legacy pair unchanged. Opaque ids: file seed is cleaned (plain slugs unchanged), path seed is the raw id. No existing test expectations changed.
